      "message": {
        "content": "## 1. Insiemi, parametri e variabili decisionali\n\n### Insiemi\n\n- Nodi:\n\\[\nN=\\{S,A,B,C,T\\}.\n\\]\n\n- Archi orientati:\n\\[\nE=\\{(S,A),(S,B),(A,B),(A,C),(B,C),(B,T),(C,T)\\}.\n\\]\n\nPer ogni nodo \\(i\\), siano \\(\\delta^+(i)\\) e \\(\\delta^-(i)\\) rispettivamente gli archi uscenti ed entranti.\n\n### Parametri\n\nPer ogni arco \\((i,j)\\in E\\):\n\n- \\(f_{ij}\\): costo fisso di attivazione;\n- \\(c_{ij}\\): costo di trasporto per unità;\n- \\(u_{ij}\\): capacità.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccc}\n(i,j) & f_{ij} & c_{ij} & u_{ij}\\\\ \\hline\n(S,A)&40&2&30\\\\\n(S,B)&35&3&35\\\\\n(A,B)&15&1&15\\\\\n(A,C)&30&2&25\\\\\n(B,C)&18&2&20\\\\\n(B,T)&45&4&25\\\\\n(C,T)&38&2&35\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nIl bilancio dei nodi è:\n\n\\[\nb_S=40,\\qquad b_T=-40,\\qquad b_A=b_B=b_C=0.\n\\]\n\n### Variabili decisionali\n\nPer ogni \\((i,j)\\in E\\):\n\n\\[\nx_{ij}\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge 0}\n\\]\n\nè il flusso intero inviato sull’arco \\((i,j)\\), mentre\n\n\\[\ny_{ij}\\in\\{0,1\\}\n\\]\n\nvale 1 se l’arco \\((i,j)\\) viene attivato, 0 altrimenti.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Formulazione matematica completa\n\n### Funzione obiettivo\n\n\\[\n\\min \\quad\n\\sum_{(i,j)\\in E}\\left(f_{ij}y_{ij}+c_{ij}x_{ij}\\right).\n\\]\n\nEsplicitamente:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\min\\quad\n&40y_{SA}+2x_{SA}\n+35y_{SB}+3x_{SB}\n+15y_{AB}+x_{AB}\\\\\n&+30y_{AC}+2x_{AC}\n+18y_{BC}+2x_{BC}\\\\\n&+45y_{BT}+4x_{BT}\n+38y_{CT}+2x_{CT}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n### Conservazione del flusso\n\nIn forma generale:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{(i,j)\\in\\delta^+(i)}x_{ij}\n-\n\\sum_{(j,i)\\in\\delta^-(i)}x_{ji}\n=b_i\n\\qquad \\forall i\\in N.\n\\]\n\nEsplicitamente:\n\n\\[\nx_{SA}+x_{SB}=40,\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_{AB}+x_{AC}-x_{SA}=0,\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_{BC}+x_{BT}-x_{SB}-x_{AB}=0,\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_{CT}-x_{AC}-x_{BC}=0,\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-x_{BT}-x_{CT}=-40.\n\\]\n\n### Capacità e attivazione degli archi\n\n\\[\nx_{ij}\\le u_{ij}y_{ij}\n\\qquad \\forall (i,j)\\in E.\n\\]\n\nEsplicitamente:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{SA}&\\le30y_{SA}, & x_{SB}&\\le35y_{SB},\\\\\nx_{AB}&\\le15y_{AB}, & x_{AC}&\\le25y_{AC},\\\\\nx_{BC}&\\le20y_{BC}, & x_{BT}&\\le25y_{BT},\\\\\nx_{CT}&\\le35y_{CT}. &&\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n### Domini\n\n\\[\nx_{ij}\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0},\\qquad\ny_{ij}\\in\\{0,1\\}\n\\qquad \\forall(i,j)\\in E.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n## 3. Codice Python eseguibile con Gurobi\n\n```python\nimport gurobipy as gp\nfrom gurobipy import GRB\nimport json\n\nresult = {\n    \"status\": \"ERROR\",\n    \"objective\": None,\n    \"variables\": {}\n}\n\ntry:\n    nodes = [\"S\", \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"T\"]\n\n    arcs = [\n        (\"S\", \"A\"),\n        (\"S\", \"B\"),\n        (\"A\", \"B\"),\n        (\"A\", \"C\"),\n        (\"B\", \"C\"),\n        (\"B\", \"T\"),\n        (\"C\", \"T\")\n    ]\n\n    fixed_cost = {\n        (\"S\", \"A\"): 40,\n        (\"S\", \"B\"): 35,\n        (\"A\", \"B\"): 15,\n        (\"A\", \"C\"): 30,\n        (\"B\", \"C\"): 18,\n        (\"B\", \"T\"): 45,\n        (\"C\", \"T\"): 38\n    }\n\n    unit_cost = {\n        (\"S\", \"A\"): 2,\n        (\"S\", \"B\"): 3,\n        (\"A\", \"B\"): 1,\n        (\"A\", \"C\"): 2,\n        (\"B\", \"C\"): 2,\n        (\"B\", \"T\"): 4,\n        (\"C\", \"T\"): 2\n    }\n\n    capacity = {\n        (\"S\", \"A\"): 30,\n        (\"S\", \"B\"): 35,\n        (\"A\", \"B\"): 15,\n        (\"A\", \"C\"): 25,\n        (\"B\", \"C\"): 20,\n        (\"B\", \"T\"): 25,\n        (\"C\", \"T\"): 35\n    }\n\n    balance = {\n        \"S\": 40,\n        \"A\": 0,\n        \"B\": 0,\n        \"C\": 0,\n        \"T\": -40\n    }\n\n    env = gp.Env(empty=True)\n    env.setParam(\"OutputFlag\", 0)\n    env.start()\n\n    model = gp.Model(\"M10_rete_distributiva\", env=env)\n    model.Params.MIPGap = 0.0\n\n    x = {\n        (i, j): model.addVar(\n            lb=0,\n            vtype=GRB.INTEGER,\n            name=f\"x_{i}_{j}\"\n        )\n        for i, j in arcs\n    }\n\n    y = {\n        (i, j): model.addVar(\n            vtype=GRB.BINARY,\n            name=f\"y_{i}_{j}\"\n        )\n        for i, j in arcs\n    }\n\n    model.setObjective(\n        gp.quicksum(\n            fixed_cost[i, j] * y[i, j]\n            + unit_cost[i, j] * x[i, j]\n            for i, j in arcs\n        ),\n        GRB.MINIMIZE\n    )\n\n    for node in nodes:\n        outgoing = gp.quicksum(\n            x[i, j] for i, j in arcs if i == node\n        )\n        incoming = gp.quicksum(\n            x[i, j] for i, j in arcs if j == node\n        )\n        model.addConstr(\n            outgoing - incoming == balance[node],\n            name=f\"balance_{node}\"\n        )\n\n    for i, j in arcs:\n        model.addConstr(\n            x[i, j] <= capacity[i, j] * y[i, j],\n            name=f\"capacity_{i}_{j}\"\n        )\n\n    model.optimize()\n\n    status_names = {\n        1: \"LOADED\",\n        2: \"OPTIMAL\",\n        3: \"INFEASIBLE\",\n        4: \"INF_OR_UNBD\",\n        5: \"UNBOUNDED\",\n        6: \"CUTOFF\",\n        7: \"ITERATION_LIMIT\",\n        8: \"NODE_LIMIT\",\n        9: \"TIME_LIMIT\",\n        10: \"SOLUTION_LIMIT\",\n        11: \"INTERRUPTED\",\n        12: \"NUMERIC\",\n        13: \"SUBOPTIMAL\",\n        14: \"INPROGRESS\",\n        15: \"USER_OBJ_LIMIT\",\n        16: \"WORK_LIMIT\",\n        17: \"MEM_LIMIT\"\n    }\n\n    solver_status = status_names.get(\n        model.Status,\n        \"STATUS_\" + str(model.Status)\n    )\n\n    if model.Status == GRB.OPTIMAL:\n        variable_values = {}\n\n        for arc in arcs:\n            value = float(round(x[arc].X))\n            variable_values[x[arc].VarName] = value\n\n        for arc in arcs:\n            value = float(round(y[arc].X))\n            variable_values[y[arc].VarName] = value\n\n        result = {\n            \"status\": \"OPTIMAL\",\n            \"objective\": float(model.ObjVal),\n            \"variables\": variable_values\n        }\n    else:\n        result = {\n            \"status\": solver_status,\n            \"objective\": None,\n            \"variables\": {}\n        }\n\nexcept gp.GurobiError:\n    result = {\n        \"status\": \"ERROR\",\n        \"objective\": None,\n        \"variables\": {}\n    }\n\nprint(\"SOLUTION_JSON=\" + json.dumps(result, separators=(\",\", \":\"), allow_nan=False))\n```\n\n## 4. Sintesi della soluzione\n\nLo stato è **OPTIMAL** e il costo minimo è:\n\n\\[\nz^*=443.\n\\]\n\nI flussi non nulli sono:\n\n\\[\nx_{SA}=25,\\quad x_{SB}=15,\\quad x_{AC}=25,\\quad\nx_{BT}=15,\\quad x_{CT}=25.\n\\]\n\nGli archi attivati sono:\n\n\\[\ny_{SA}=y_{SB}=y_{AC}=y_{BT}=y_{CT}=1.\n\\]\n\nGli archi \\(A\\to B\\) e \\(B\\to C\\) non vengono attivati. Il costo totale comprende 188 unità di costi fissi e 255 unità di costi di trasporto.",
